Number 02 - Add Two Numbers
The two linked lists store the digits in reverse order, so the first node of each is the units digit, 
which allows the values to be added using column addition from the start of each list. It creates a dummy 
node to build the answer, and a pointer (current) to track the end of the list. It loops while either list 
has nodes left or there is a carry remaining. In each loop, it takes the current digit from each list, or 0 
if that list has run out of values, and adds them together with the carry. The % 10 is to get the digit from 
the addition and the // 10 is to get the carry. A new node holding the digit is added to the answer list, 
and current, l1 and l2 are all moved forward to their next nodes. It returns dummy.next, which skips the dummy 
node and gives the start of the answer.
