Number 14 - Longest Common Prefix
After finding the shortest string, as the prefix cannot be longer than it, it goes through each
character position across every word, e.g. word 1 char 1, word 2 char 1 and so on. As soon as a 
character doesnt match, it saves the position it got up to and returns the common prefix up to that
point. If every character matches, the entirety of the shortest string is returned. Alternatively, 
if nothing matches it returns an empty string.
