Number 20 - Valid Parentheses
After creating an empty list to use as a stack and a dictionary of opening brackets with the matching closing 
bracket, the code goes through the string and pushes opening brackets onto a stack. When it hits a closing 
bracket, it pops the most recent opening bracket and checks that its a matching pair. If the stack is 
empty when a closing bracket is hit, or the pair doesnt match, its invalid. At the end of the loop, the string 
is only valid if the stack is empty, meaning no open brackets were left unclosed.
